{%- comment -%}
  DAILY MANTRA — a single zen quote displayed beneath the homepage hero.
  - Quote pool lives in the {%- capture pool_raw -%} block below. One quote
    per line. Add/replace quotes anytime; the section picks ONE per day
    deterministically (day-of-year modulo pool size) so every visitor on the
    same day sees the same quote, and Shopify CDN cache stays valid.
  - Center-aligned card on a color_scheme background; serif quote stack
    (Georgia / Songti SC) gives a meditative tone.
  - Mobile quote font-size floors at 1.8rem per project hard rule.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- capture pool_raw -%}
The snow peak does not announce its height. The valley already knows.
The mountain has not moved since before your name was spoken. It waits.
White peaks hold the silence. The wind borrows it and returns nothing.
The summit does not call the climber. The climber calls the summit.
Snow falls on the still and the restless. Neither catches more.
The mountain does not hurry toward the sunrise. The sunrise arrives.
Where the snow stops, the stone begins. Neither claims the line.
The peak stands alone. So does the one who has stopped explaining.
Altitude teaches what the valley cannot hear. The wind translates.
The mountain's shadow reaches the valley before the mountain speaks.
The lake holds two skies. It does not confuse them. You do.
Still water does not search for the moon. The moon finds it.
A stone drops. The lake forgets. The ripple does not forget so quickly.
The lake reflects what you bring to the shore. Bring nothing.
Deep water makes no sound. The shallow current shouts at the banks.
The pond waits for the moon. The moon does not know it is waited for.
Water shapes the stone by patience. The stone calls it erosion. The water calls it friendship.
Frozen water still remembers flowing. It does not say so aloud.
Stillness is not the absence of movement. It is presence without noise.
The lake keeps its depth hidden. The surface is for strangers.
The wind moves the prayer flag. The flag moves nothing in return.
Wind has no destination. It has direction. The difference is everything.
The wind does not explain itself to the trees it bends. Neither should you.
What the wind touches, it lets go. That is why it travels so far.
The wind carves the canyon not by striking. By leaving.
A gust arrives without warning. A thought departs without permission.
The wind does not choose where it goes. It chooses to go.
Flags fray in the wind. The prayer written on them does not fray.
Still air is not wind that stopped. It is patience that has not yet moved.
Wind reads the land. The land does not read back. The wind does not mind.
The moon does not try to shine. It does not need to try.
Moonlight reaches the valley the mountain cannot. Softness travels where height stops.
The moon borrows light and keeps no debt. The ocean moves anyway.
A full moon asks nothing. A new moon answers nothing. Both are complete.
The crescent holds less than the full moon. It shines with the same confidence.
Moonlight on snow. Two kinds of white. One source neither owns.
The moon waits for no one. It waits for everyone. There is no contradiction.
Under the same moon, two strangers kneel. Neither knows the other is heard.
The moon does not own its light. You do not own your gifts. Shine anyway.
The moon moves the tide without lifting a hand. Influence is not force.
The lamp burns. The name written beside it remains. The oil does not.
A flame has no opinion about the dark. It simply rises.
The butter lamp melts itself to give light. It does not calculate the cost.
One lamp lights a thousand. It does not lose its flame in the sharing.
The wick does not know what it holds. It holds the fire regardless.
Wind tests the flame. The flame tests the wind. Neither surrenders quietly.
The lamp gives what it has. It gives until what it has is gone.
A flame does not compare itself to the sun. It is busy burning.
When the lamp goes out, the room does not forget where the light stood.
The lamp's shadow is longer than its flame. So is the intention behind the gift.
Flags fade in the sun. The wind reads them anyway, faded or new.
Five colors. One wind. One prayer repeated until the thread forgets the words.
The flag does not hold the wind. The wind holds the flag. The difference is surrender.
Frayed threads still carry intention. The fraying is not the failure.
The prayer flag has no anchor. It has a rope. That is enough.
Colors bleed into rain. Prayers do not bleed. They soak in.
The flag is cloth. The wind is not. The blessing is neither and both.
A hundred flags. One sky. No confusion about which is heard.
The flag points where the wind has already been. It does not point ahead.
When the last thread breaks, the prayer has already arrived. The rope is not the message.
The eagle does not flap to stay aloft. It finds the current and trusts it.
Wings hold nothing. They release everything into the wind they cannot control.
The eagle sees the field and the cliff in one glance. You choose one.
Height does not make the eagle. The eagle makes the height by choosing to rise.
The shadow crosses the ground. The eagle does not follow the shadow down.
An eagle lands only to leave again. Rest is not the destination.
The circling is not hesitation. It is reading the wind's handwriting.
The eagle carries no map. It carries trust in the current it cannot see.
Feathers know the wind better than the wind knows itself. The eagle knows the feathers.
The eagle descends with purpose. It does not explain the purpose to the field.
Where water arrives, the story follows. Water does not wait for the story.
The river does not ask the mountain for permission to pass. It passes.
Water finds the path by losing itself in it. The path is the losing.
The river forgets its source. The source remembers the river. Memory flows upstream.
A stream does not compare itself to the great river. Both arrive at the same sea.
The river carries the mountain's gift downstream. The mountain does not send a note.
Water has no shape. It takes the shape of everything that holds it and leaves.
The riverbed holds the river. The river does not notice the riverbed. That is trust.
Where two rivers meet, neither argues about the name. They become one current.
The river reaches the sea and becomes the sea. It does not mourn the river.
The stone sits. The world moves around it. The stone does not comment.
Moss grows on patience. So does stone. The stone does not hurry the moss.
A rock does not roll uphill. It does not need to. Downhill is also a destination.
The stone holds the mountain's weight. You hold less. You complain more.
Gravel speaks to the river. Boulder listens. Both are right.
The stone does not say it was a mountain once. It does not need to.
Rain wears the stone thin. The stone wears the rain invisible. Both are changed.
A stone in a riverbed has no name. It has a position. That is enough.
The cairn is built by strangers. It points the same way for all of them.
The stone and the seed share a patience. The seed wins. The stone does not mind.
Fog hides the path. The path is still there. The fog does not erase the path.
The mist does not erase the mountain. It asks you to trust the mountain is there.
Fog has no center. You do. The fog is a reminder to find it.
The cloud descends to the valley. The valley does not notice the promotion.
Mist makes neighbors of strangers. Clarity does the opposite. Both are necessary.
Fog is water that forgot to fall. It remembers eventually. Everything does.
In the fog, the lamp is closer than it looks. Trust the lamp, not the fog.
The mist lifts. What was there was always there. You were the one who could not see.
Clouds do not own the sky. They pass through it. The sky does not charge rent.
When the fog clears, you see what you already knew. The fog was not hiding it. The fog was hiding you.
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- assign pool_lines = pool_raw | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
{%- assign mantra_pool_string = '' -%}
{%- for line in pool_lines -%}
  {%- assign trimmed = line | strip -%}
  {%- if trimmed != blank and trimmed != '' -%}
    {%- assign first_char = trimmed | slice: 0 -%}
    {%- if first_char != '#' -%}
      {%- assign mantra_pool_string = mantra_pool_string | append: '|||' | append: trimmed -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if mantra_pool_string != '' -%}
  {%- assign mantra_pool_string = mantra_pool_string | remove_first: '|||' -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign mantra_pool = mantra_pool_string | split: '|||' -%}
{%- assign mantra_count = mantra_pool | size -%}

{%- assign day_of_year = 'now' | date: '%j' | plus: 0 -%}
{%- assign today_index = day_of_year | modulo: mantra_count -%}
{%- assign today_mantra = '' -%}
{%- assign i = 0 -%}
{%- for q in mantra_pool -%}
  {%- if i == today_index -%}
    {%- assign today_mantra = q -%}
    {%- break -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- assign i = i | plus: 1 -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{{ 'section-daily-mantra.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- style -%}
  .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
    padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
    padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
      padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;
      padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
    }
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

<div class="daily-mantra color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} gradient isolate{% unless section.settings.full_width %} page-width{% endunless %}">
  <div class="daily-mantra__inner section-{{ section.id }}-padding">
    {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
      <p
        class="daily-mantra__eyebrow{% if settings.animations_reveal_on_scroll %} scroll-trigger animate--slide-in{% endif %}"
        {% if settings.animations_reveal_on_scroll %}
          data-cascade
          style="--animation-order: 1;"
        {% endif %}
      >
        {{ section.settings.eyebrow | escape }}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.show_divider -%}
      <div
        class="daily-mantra__divider{% if settings.animations_reveal_on_scroll %} scroll-trigger animate--slide-in{% endif %}"
        aria-hidden="true"
        {% if settings.animations_reveal_on_scroll %}
          data-cascade
          style="--animation-order: 2;"
        {% endif %}
      >
        <span class="daily-mantra__divider-mark">{{ section.settings.divider_mark }}</span>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if today_mantra != blank -%}
      <div
        class="daily-mantra__quote{% if settings.animations_reveal_on_scroll %} scroll-trigger animate--slide-in{% endif %}"
        {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
        {% if settings.animations_reveal_on_scroll %}
          data-cascade
          style="--animation-order: 3;"
        {% endif %}
      >
        {{ today_mantra | escape }}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.attribution != blank -%}
      <p
        class="daily-mantra__attribution{% if settings.animations_reveal_on_scroll %} scroll-trigger animate--slide-in{% endif %}"
        {% if settings.animations_reveal_on_scroll %}
          data-cascade
          style="--animation-order: 4;"
        {% endif %}
      >
        {{ section.settings.attribution | escape }}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Daily Mantra",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header", "footer"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Content"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The quote pool is built into sections/daily-mantra.liquid (look for the MANTRA POOL block at the top of the file). Add one quote per line; the section picks one quote per day automatically — no manual daily update needed."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow label",
      "default": "DAILY MANTRA",
      "info": "Small uppercase label above the quote."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "attribution",
      "label": "Attribution (optional)",
      "default": "— Kailash Way Daily Reflection",
      "info": "Source or sign-off line beneath the quote. Leave blank to hide."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_divider",
      "label": "Show decorative divider",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "divider_mark",
      "label": "Divider mark",
      "default": "❖",
      "info": "A small glyph centered in the divider line."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "full_width",
      "label": "Make section full width",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "Color scheme",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Section padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Top padding",
      "default": 56
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Bottom padding",
      "default": 56
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Daily Mantra",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "DAILY MANTRA",
        "attribution": "— Kailash Way Daily Reflection",
        "show_divider": true,
        "divider_mark": "❖",
        "full_width": true,
        "color_scheme": "scheme-1",
        "padding_top": 56,
        "padding_bottom": 56
      }
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
